/-!
# The actual transvection-generated centralizer quotient in the solvable seed branch

The marked conjugate center has the same cyclic image on VH as on U-hat:
its hatted kernel lies in U and hence centralizes VH. Thus the image of
K = <Z(U)^g^H> in H/C_H(VH) is the normal closure of the original surviving
rank-one involution. Reducedness makes its two-core trivial. The local H
supplies an actual SQTK cover, so the proved B.5 classification applies to
the faithful K-action on the original VH, including its fixed vectors.

The relative quotient K/C_K(VH) is identified with that exact image, with
its evaluation on each element of K. No identification with S3 is inferred
from surjectivity alone. Selecting the S3 row, splitting the whole Z(U),
and completing 14.3.25 and 14.3.31 remain with this centerlessness owner.
The earlier marked SolvableSeedRow remains an explicit source obligation;
the later action theorem assuming centerlessness cannot discharge it.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 14.3.25, printed p.1001, B.5.3--6, pp.104--105,
and the normal-closure step of G.6.4, pp.345--346.
-/

public noncomputable section
